 Call the Skill tool twice, for "grilling" and "domain-modeling".
+
+Put each round's questions through the `AskUserQuestion` tool rather than
+writing them as prose. The round structure is unchanged: still the whole
+frontier at once, still a recommendation per question.
+
+- The tool takes at most 4 questions per call, so a wider round goes out as
+  consecutive calls in the same turn. Do not drop questions to fit.
+- The `➡️` recommendation becomes the first option, labelled `(Recommended)`.
+- Each question takes 2 to 4 options. Where the answer is open rather than a
+  choice, offer the plausible answers anyway; the tool always adds a free-text
+  option, so nothing is lost by asking this way.
+- Set `multiSelect: true` when the choices are not exclusive.
+- Use `preview` when the options are things to look at rather than read, such
+  as competing layouts, schemas, or code shapes.
